  "id": "computerized-therapy",
  "term": "computerized therapy",
  "definition": "Computerized therapy is a low-intensity form of care based on cognitive-behavioral therapy and delivered through a computer rather than relying as heavily on direct therapist involvement. It is used to provide more accessible support, especially for mild to moderate mental health problems.",
